 ],
 "vendor_website": "stiebel-eltron.com",
 "description": "Internet Service Gateway ISG web and ISG plus with the Modbus TCP/IP software extension: heat pump manager WPM 3 and WPM 3i system values, parameters, status and energy data",
 "revision": 2,
 "revised": "2026-11-14",
 "source": "Stiebel Eltron, Software documentation Modbus TCP/IP (Software extension for Internet Service Gateway), WPM 3 / WPM 3i chapter and chapter 10",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Software documentation Modbus TCP/IP: Software extension for Internet Service Gateway",
   "date": "2026-06",
   "url": "https://www.stiebel-eltron.com/content/dam/ste/cdbassets/current/commissioning_manual/commissioning_manual_doc-00081716.pdf",
   "note": "linked in issue #200; chapter 7 (WPM 3 and WPM 3i), chapter 10 (SG Ready); no version is printed, the PDF was generated in June 2026"
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Addresses are the numbers of the manufacturer's tables (for example 501 for 30501). The document says the ISG is one-based and that an offset of 1 may be needed depending on the client, so address_base is 1: the address on the wire is the number minus 1. If a read returns the neighbouring value, try address_base 0.",
  "The register tables differ per controller: the manufacturer publishes separate tables for WPMsystem, WPM 3 / WPM 3i, LWZ (05.1, 07.1) Plus (ISG Connect only), integral ventilation units and WPM G (WPE-I). This map follows only the WPM 3 / WPM 3i tables plus the SG Ready registers; the numbers in other tables can mean something else.",
  "Not every object exists on every device. An object that is not available reads 32768 (0x8000), shown here as a sentinel.",
  "Temperatures and most setpoints are integers with a 0.1 scale; the values with data type 7 (pressures, heating curve slope, volume flow) use 0.01. Energy totals are split: total energy = MWh register × 1000 + kWh register (0-999).",
  "The per-heat-pump values (addresses 542-583, 3523 onward), the cooling-circuit setpoints of WPMsystem, the fixed-value mode (1508), the reset registers (1520, 1521) and the power-limitation registers (4250 onward) are not in this map.",
  "Default connection: IP 192.168.0.126 when connected directly, TCP port 502, slave ID 1 (cannot be changed). Modbus TCP/IP needs the Basic service package and cannot be combined with other ISG software interfaces, apart from read access next to the EMI extension.",
  "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
 ],
